          "complete_text_SHA256": "06e1ad5833b4e7957fef316f31eb27adb377ca3b268d958df9803c6a903bc84e",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 1–2. Confirmed the exact v4 title, both full authors, arXiv revision stamp 13 September 2026, and the seventy-four-page paper structure. The abstract announces all-field normalized packet realizations, Lorentzianity/generalized-polymatroid support and intrinsic Chern-moment Hodge statements; these are source claims only at this stage, with no proof credit or book admission. The contents locate volume constructions at pages 9–37, moment/tropical/nonvanishing sections at 38–58, appendices at 59–70, AI-use statement at 71 and references at 72–74."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:50:45.434751+00:00",
          "sheet": 2,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            3,
            4
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "5d44921e7c70c0e33fd87e939cd22c43184dc05533f2aa01b4b7c9fcca2485db",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "6f70fbf9aa91117732650eaf77119a8ef2e0915c1625e8dd8f002b21c46fb7e2",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the full text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 3–4. RV_k is exact nonnegative rational top-intersection realization on an integral projective variety over the original field with semiample Cartier classes, not a closed coefficient-limit cone. Homogeneous packets place Q_k(x) of degree d+k beside z^(L-k). Recorded the explicit K_i^(z), barred K_i^(z)=K_i^(z)-z id, and D_i^(z) divided-difference conventions, rightmost-first action, seed x^lambda/x^delta, sign-corrected ordinary Grothendieck layers and minimal excess r_w. Theorem 1.1 announces all-field realization of all three normalized packets; its proof has not yet been read. Distinguish coefficient geometry from representing a Schubert cohomology class and retain the cited conjectures' exact historical scope."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:51:45.459229+00:00",
          "sheet": 3,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            5,
            6
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "c443fab5909489e77c4993777d0e0f5f11c07360d63d8f72e3a19bf7714c1f4e",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "62d5efd49912445f973deed841166831009134139f5d0dbe7c0b1b9cdb920610",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching rendered image for physical pages 5–6. Theorem 1.1 continues with layer/minimal-padding removal by divided-power differentiation and z=0, nonzero Lorentzian/algebraic-polymatroid support, characteristic-zero smoothness and ordinary signed-support M-natural-convexity. The source explicitly excludes double-Schubert and separate coefficient/schubitope questions. Example 1.2 has N(H)=[z(x+y)^2+xy(x+y)]/2; the fraction covers the entire numerator. The raw quadratic Hessian has eigenvalues 3 and 1. The introductory Chern-flow mechanism absorbs kernel top factors via Whitney identities without inversion; creation time must be retained as well as rank. Row/co-row generated bundles, terminal balance, finite-box reciprocal reversal and the integral evaluation-kernel incidence route are announced, with their actual propositions still to be read."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:53:04.013903+00:00",
          "sheet": 4,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            7,
            8
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "22736353af47ec02d8fa103930919b84242f7c7276f9ea3298d59558f3be907f",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "45077dc172196f01ecb1d02645128a55c61c3a36a2e4dcc3f4975e891b9fcd17",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching rendered image for physical pages 7–8. The skew-Schur paper is explicitly not a proof input. Theorem 1.3 concerns the intrinsic joint-moment quotient of the full real even Hodge-class algebra of a smooth integral complex projective variety, with L Kähler and all t_i strictly positive. Chern-index variables are not substitutions by c1(E_i). The weighted top-Chern quotient requires a nonzero product and uses formal dimension d-sum ranks. The source distinguishes all-degree moment-algebra Hodge relations from individual original Chern-class assertions and from the smaller scalar apolar algebra (Example 6.17). Theorem 1.4 uses smooth projective fans and globally generated Kaveh–Manon bundles without representability; its Lorentzian statement permits zero and nef divisor directions. Equivariant inverse-Chern comparison only becomes the ordinary identity after global characters vanish in Chow. Proofs/descent and matroid certificates remain to be read, not admitted as verified results yet."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:53:41.926589+00:00",
          "sheet": 5,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            9,
            10
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "964dbf2f642ec40a54ecd615d5be620fe1674449a23d2b02a86ddd49a83aa25a",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "71a15f2330fdc5684cfa01306d1c0065d85213331de9da03b9809856818b1aa4",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the full text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 9–10. The nonrepresentable tropical case explicitly supplies a Hodge algebra rather than a geometric volume model or an asserted exact tropical-bundle sequence. The source announces the subset Chern nonvanishing rank criterion, algebraic clone matroids in the geometric case and descended-pairing equality tests, to be checked later. Part 1 is independent of Part 2, avoiding a circular use of the new moment-algebra statements in the volume proof. All coefficients/differential operators and Chow products are rational regardless of geometric characteristic; factorials are not inverted in the field. Verified the divided-power derivative and finite-box reciprocal involution formulas, larger-cap translation, simultaneous M-convex exchange definition, closed Lorentzian conventions including zero, and the normalized coefficient Hessian H_beta=(c_(beta+e_i+e_j)). The varying-degree lift retains D at least the maximum coordinate sum."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:54:58.715886+00:00",
          "sheet": 6,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            11,
            12
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "bd6efe996e42f5e3e17e39a4459e0394bf56ac950a269470ee53ba10344792a0",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "05a49c64115cb204304a2fc9051fda6aa17c137e056655d6d500602b5ae7f4fe",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 11–12. Lemma 2.3's displayed proof uses the affine lattice slack embedding and distinct homogeneous x-degrees, so nonzero signed layer weights do not cancel support; the parameter support is related by an affine unimodular map. Definition 2.4 allows zero through a rational scalar and integral projective exact realizations. Proposition 2.5 attributes all-field permutations, rational nonnegative substitutions, differentiation, polarization and reversible divided-power translation to GHMSW Theorem 1.3/Proposition 4.1/Remark 1.14, already fully read at the preceding source checkpoint; it uses resolution only for characteristic-zero smooth realization. Proposition 2.6 derives algebraic-polymatroid and polarized clone-matroid support from GHMSW Proposition 5.4, retaining the actual base field. Linear representations over an extension are explicitly kept separate. Recorded Gamma, Pi, K and D operator conventions and common-box dependency; no new universal operator preservation theorem is inferred from them."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:55:57.608335+00:00",
          "sheet": 7,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            13,
            14
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "161e902bf47377d91ec859eaeb8dedb44a5a132fe39638658b1be8a8de98618d",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "b9fa388f0f10ebe98e6f80b34d23cbdf5ce289569ee72f45c855329b90cd0c23",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the full text and individually inspected the matching rendered image for physical pages 13–14. Remark 2.7 explicitly denies that ordinary differential-preserver results prove Demazure or opposite-Demazure preservation; operator-word rightmost-first and key/permutation conventions are retained. Checked the quotient-projectivization sign p_*(xi^(r-1+m))=h_m(E), inverse c_-t series and cycle/operational distinction over singular sources. Read the entire Proposition 2.8 proof: pad generating sections to positive kernel rank s, use integral Z=P(K^dual), H semiample, M=s+R-1 and dim Z=d_X+M-R. The identity c_-t(K^dual)c_t(V)=1 gives p_*H^M=c_R(V); the projection formula and ordinary y-derivative extract the finite-box dual coefficient polynomial without an extra factorial. Nonzero pushforward enforces 0<=c<=dim B; zero is treated separately. Incidence smoothness for smooth X is not the same as asserting all-field smoothness of every final derivative model; final smooth realization is stated in characteristic zero. The proof avoids assuming an integral general zero scheme, as the O_P1(2) example emphasizes."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:56:46.164996+00:00",
          "sheet": 8,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            15,
            16
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "6f4b149e47388263d7fc7e4cdbcb7203375b6d6bfb728d6c70655b32c5da1579",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "b2f12f68aa5be4504d4e64319a573d5ee64641b5798b168e43b5bc040e549658",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the full text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 15–16. Read the complete Proposition 2.10 proof over the original arbitrary field: positive kernel ranks, integral iterated quotient projective bundles, generated tautological classes, flat-base-change compatibility and h_a(K_i^dual)=c_a(E_i) give the shifted divided-power volume identity; coordinate derivatives remove the shifts. Zero and singular integral sources are included; smooth realization remains restricted to characteristic zero. This matches the previously integrated complex Chern calculation while explicitly retaining the stronger attributed base-field scope. Read the canonical inverse-Lehmer row-word definition and full Lemma 3.1 proof by descending placement of values; row lengths sum to the inversion number of u inverse. The 3412 example is word (2,3 | 1,2). Recorded the finite product-of-projective-spaces base, generated split L_i/M directions and initial prefix quotient flag; bundle generation along the tower remains to be read."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T20:58:12.975344+00:00",
          "sheet": 9,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            17,
