          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "bbdf7d9dac0ec687b8a05c8f624517d9eff279ebb0dd27cf967a10184c14e30c",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "d4c7208826e59fafca728a50b6d732c36d42c64ffca44c50d90df66676dc0390",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the full text and individually inspected the matching rendered image for physical pages 17–18. Checked the actual quotient-flag tower construction: rank-two K_t is a kernel of a surjection between prefix bundles, P(K_t) uses quotient convention, and F_i^(t)=F_(i+1)^(t-1)/S_t is locally free. The displayed commutative exact-row diagram supplies both neighbouring quotient maps and the exact S_t/Q_t sequences. Every time-indexed prefix remains a generated quotient of the pullback of E, but this does not assert generation of its individual kernel lines. The smooth geometrically irreducible projective tower is an iterated P1 bundle over the finite box. The relative flag Cartesian square is explanatory rather than a proof input. Recorded actual root lines, their ordered replacement by (q_t,s_t), the nonsplit rank-two extension, and the p_(b,a) pullback convention. The Gysin formula (3.16) is stated at the page end; its proof is on the following sheet and has not yet received reading credit."
        },
        {
