          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 23–24. Completed Proposition 4.1: the K0 sum of edge exact sequences yields divergence multiplicities, equal ranks and equality of total Chern series; inverses here have constant term one and do not invert a top Chern class. Equal total rank permits the top-component factorization. Nonnegative divergence gives an actual generated direct sum; no acyclicity or path matching is needed for this identity. Definition 4.3 identifies only passive pullbacks of the same created rank-j prefix. Definition 4.4 retains all actual creation states; edge directions are new rank-i state to the then-current rank-(i+1) state, with terminal multiplicities supplied by root edges. Such tower edges increase rank and hence are acyclic. Inspected Example 4.5's 3412 graph, including two distinct rank-two and rank-three states and their composable paths. The canonical-word balance criterion has only been introduced; its proof is on the next sheet."
