          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 25–26. Read Lemma 4.6's full canonical-row balance proof: each nonfinal created rank-j state receives the colour-(j-1) edge immediately before the next occurrence of j, while a final state needs terminal multiplicity exactly when its last occurrence follows the last j-1 occurrence. Initial states and rank n have no outgoing demand. Staircase differences one suffice for all-kernel profiles. Read the complete Theorem 4.7 construction: realized time-indexed exact sequences yield the canonical generated divergence sum U, and the completed generated row bundles twisted by M supply all q+z factors. The generated V has rank ell+|mu|+sum epsilon, so pushforward codimension is |mu|+sum epsilon. A support-containing box including z makes the Chow representative unique; Proposition 2.8 then realizes its normalized finite dual over the original field. This proves reciprocal covariance for balanced profiles, including epsilon=0 for every partition and epsilon=1 only with the stated balance condition (in particular the staircase), rather than unrestricted operator preservation."
