          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 27–28. Section 5 treats three different reciprocal operator families and explicitly does not use general finite-complement preservation. Recorded K=z*pi+x_i*x_(i+1)*partial_i and D=z*d_i^(z^-1), with braid identities attributed to the listed original sources. Read Lemma 5.1's full monomial proof: both source operators retain a common x-coordinate cap M while increasing the z cap by at most one, including negative divided-difference cases. Defined equal-x-cap raw reciprocal R_(M,r) and variable reversal omega. Lemma 5.2 states the local transports R K R=1-(x_i+z)partial_i, R barK R=-(x_i+z)partial_i and R D R=-K, becoming Pi, barPi and Gamma^(1,z) under reversal. Word transport must match the successive z caps. The proof of Lemma 5.2 lies on the next page and is not yet credited as read."
