          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 41–42. Read Proposition 6.6 in full: surjectivity to B and B duality identify the multiplication-annihilator with Ann_B(eta), so marked intrinsicness follows independently of auxiliary ranks. A positive inverse-Chern certificate additionally requires the full Kähler package and all relative generators in its closed cone; an algebraic inverse recurrence alone does not suffice. Read Proposition 6.8 and Corollaries 6.9–6.10: nonzero fibre-top eta permits boundary descent; out-of-range moments kill z_i^(r_i+1); the product z_i^r_i is nonzero exactly when the top Chern product theta is nonzero, and the further quotient is A/Ann(theta) with relative generators zero. Read Proposition 6.11's entire geometric proof. It uses the real diagonal Hodge-class algebra, not arbitrary Chow duality, and the evaluation-kernel dual projective bundles with ranks padded at least two. Projective-bundle signs cancel, semipositive Fubini–Study representatives plus a base Kähler form are positive, and the resulting open cone gives the certificate. Final all-degree HR still depends on the precise external boundary-descent lemma; weighted-base dimension d-sum ranks requires nonzero theta."
