          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 49–50. Read Lemma 7.4's matroid exchange/tangent-cone proof that each adapted basis is maximum for the circuit-minimum coordinate weights. The witness matroid restricts and duplicates basis elements in parallel, with two zero-weight loops padding dual rank at least two. Proposition 7.5's full argument converts maximum primal witnesses to minimum dual bases by complementation. Theorem 7.6's full proof gives equivariant K*C equal to the global-character product; only passage to ordinary Chow makes it the inverse identity, and the positive relative sign remains +xi. Proposition 7.7 uses the simultaneous Larson–Partida presentation and boundary descent to obtain the intrinsic tropical moment package, Lorentzian joint Chern/nef polynomial and top-Chern weighted base quotient; only ample spanning base directions recover the full apolar algebra. This proves a nonrepresentable combinatorial certificate conditional on the exact external input, without a geometric kernel or tropical exact sequence. Corollary 7.8 states Chern-number nonnegativity/log-concavity and interval support; its proof is on the next page."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:08:29.249039+00:00",
          "sheet": 26,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            51,
            52
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "aa66ac1be5149a588ccf5496c3d578623cdecc90fa813f091741415279e38810",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "095e9256b45b3bff476443cabd19587adb5197b20df07c30764113bcba0f18a4",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 51–52. Completed Corollary 7.8: the binary divided-power criterion gives unweighted coefficient log-concavity, positivity and interval support; ample H has a0>0, whereas nef boundary permits zero. The source claims to settle Kaveh–Manon Conjecture 1.7; the original conjecture remains an external status dependency. Read the adapted weighted presentation and Proposition 7.10's closure-envelope construction, with the opposite Ardila sign and maximum-basis formula explicitly imported. It classifies Chern data, not bundle isomorphism classes. Propositions 7.11–7.12 give finite ray single-exchange tests and a full-label duality (P,u)->(P*, -u); loops must be retained for involutivity and deleted only for the loopless envelope. Ordinary inverse Chern identities are distinct from equivariant global-character products. Proposition 7.13 requires rank-marked Whitney series identities and an adapted terminal presentation; it yields the terminal moment/weighted packages without claiming tropical kernels, cokernels or exact evaluation sequences. No top Chern class is divided."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:08:48.590439+00:00",
          "sheet": 27,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            53,
            54
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "ac3653c19e9b0970ff427c0624b4e87223f65b03da9dc09249f0c1747097bbbd",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "2f472050510cc18f1947519d2ce35a6bf828fa914ba4572d7f8b35f55b985a18",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 53–54. Section 7 explicitly limits the comparison to KM objects on stated smooth projective toric bases, excludes general valuated matroids and arbitrary Hodge pushforwards/sums, and notes that the terminal matroid Chow identification is not an independent proof of matroid Hodge theory. Read Lemma 8.1's full effectivity argument over complex smooth X: a generated twisted direct sum on a product of projective spaces has a smooth general zero scheme (possibly empty, not assumed integral), whose effective pushforward represents the desired Chern product. Positive ample degree detects its rational Chow and real cycle-class nonvanishing. This is distinct from Part 1's all-field integral incidence route. Read Lemma 8.2's numerical substitute using degree-one generation, nonnegative mixed degrees and ample domination; it applies to the toric Chow algebra without representability. Theorem 8.3 states subset rank inequalities for all joint Chern products and begins its slack-support proof; completion is on page 55."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:09:14.143010+00:00",
          "sheet": 28,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            55,
            56
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "f6fdc2a265e006db1914ecfb6a5947559907319bc5fe017e89e60130101480c5",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "32efc3ae33c6d4a5ecde4cf8c01e7eea92707dd34dc71c10400a32e003fe0413",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 55–56. Completed Theorem 8.3: pure slack coefficient makes the projected M-convex support an independence polymatroid, and ample detection plus Whitney's nonnegative summands identifies its rank with the largest nonzero Chern index of each direct sum. Read Proposition 8.5's full residual-rank proof via supersets and submodularity, including associative residual updates. Read Proposition 8.6's full geometric clone-matroid argument: add H^direct-sum-d as a slack bundle, polarize exact total-Chern volume, delete the slack basis, and use augmentation plus ample detection to characterize every labelled clone set. Its contraction algebraicity invokes GHMSW Corollary 5.6 and is not claimed for arbitrary tropical nonrepresentable data. Remark 8.7 separates active-index contraction c_(alpha+beta) from fixed insertion c_alpha*c_beta. Corollary 8.8 begins normalized coefficient Hessian/minor and cross-layer inequalities for original unnormalized coefficients; the proof and final conditions follow on page 57."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:09:36.300256+00:00",
          "sheet": 29,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            57,
            58
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "d9748bc7e6f9fb3d1b0b622f5a329ee8240c19a3d68a22410e7df481967ff061",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "9656c209012e40724aa64d75a3bfc0f00768eddc73dadd4eee70b25cb021760d",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 57–58. Completed Corollary 8.8's matrix proof: nonnegative nonzero symmetric principal matrices have a positive Rayleigh quotient, so the at-most-one-positive condition gives determinant signs and root-line coefficient log-concavity with saturated interval support. Proposition 8.9 imports the binomial reverse Khovanskii–Teissier inequality from Jiang–Li Theorem 1.1, already fully read in the prior frozen source checkpoint; no fresh dependency credit is assigned. Proposition 8.10 uses real nonnegative substitution and the binary criterion to prove log-concavity of multinomially weighted excess-layer masses, explicitly not unweighted sums. Read Proposition 8.11's full surface-pairing proof of equality and the quantitative Cauchy–Schwarz bound. Read Corollary 8.12's whole annihilator equality argument: a_(i-1)>0 ensures nonzero boundary descent eta_i, and equality is a relation in the surface quotient, not bundle splitting. The concluding geometric/toric specialization continues on page 59."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:09:57.539142+00:00",
          "sheet": 30,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            59,
            60
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "97add5396059dcd25a2cbb03b88a7171f3d5c67f9bf42eb33fccb3e09252ce28",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "fc3d0aa4a321bb0714beb110ccc73b8f92bb5b930eca052d265212b27abbc103",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 59–60. Completed the equality boundary example: the rank-two quotient on P2 has sequence (1,1,1) but cannot split into two line bundles with a+b=1 and ab=1. Read Appendix A in full, completing the deferred local reciprocal proof: conjugating a divided difference gives -xy*partial, mixed z caps turn multiplication by z into identity, and K=z+y(x+z)partial/D=-id+(x+z)partial give the stated source transports. Intermediate Laurent multiplication is permitted; the final capped identities are polynomial identities, not merely Chow truncations. Read Proposition B.1's whole arbitrary-word weighted balance criterion. Internal deficits cannot be repaired by terminal edges, and the least terminal completion is the final outgoing weight minus its later incoming supply, truncated at zero. The canonical-row volume application retains that hypothesis and its labelled creation states; K0 equality alone supplies no canonical bundle isomorphism. The weighted differential/support consequences start next."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:10:19.528765+00:00",
          "sheet": 31,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            61,
            62
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "6d5268d4b69e25e95102689ebc80cce7f69ba3bff8d6e71dbc59acb1b25920a3",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "efa7a240a5995420859b9db37af45c83790a7bbbe308f6bdbca2bd8d0f902302",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 61–62. Corollary B.2 identifies a balanced weighted polynomial's ordinary constant-coefficient differential operator as realizable covolume through P(partial)y^[m]=D_m N(P); it invokes the previously read GHMSW all-field preserver theorem, including spectators and zero, and does not concern divided-difference/Demazure preservation. Corollary B.3 proves reflected M-convex saturated support and its cap-independent rank formula without asserting volume realizability of the original weighted coefficients. Read Proposition B.4's entire characteristic-zero reflection proof: differential subspaces linearize finitely generated algebraic ranks, a kernel projection dualizes the rank, and simultaneous minor-preserving specialization gives a finite algebraic field extension, or the original algebraically closed field. Linear forms then preserve algebraicity over the original k. The characteristic-zero restriction and possible finite extension are essential; no positive-characteristic algebraic-duality claim follows. External differential/Nullstellensatz references support the displayed elementary proof and remain cited foundations, not new independent certification."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:10:35.514737+00:00",
          "sheet": 32,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            63,
            64
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "111e42c900e955ff9e87fecbc20f70eb75f95769712ed3ed7159748c5fc049ea",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "522787365e2a99df151f49257d6360b7fd22390d476fd3f8a7f865b610a750ab",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 63–64. Remark B.5 explicitly excludes general divided-difference preservation, original weighted-coefficient volume/Lorentzianity and unrestricted positive-characteristic algebraic duality. Read relative Propositions B.6–B.7 in full: quotient rows allow nonincreasing starts with generated initial tails ker(E->F_(a-1)), whereas old-upper-root co-rows require strictly decreasing starts and generated ker(E->F_a). Their actual generation proofs preserve the required unchanged prefixes; individual row twists are tied to the specified word. The repeated (1,1) trivial-rank-two example produces O(-1) as the second co-row tail, explaining the strictness. Factorial normalization does not commute with identifying twist variables, demonstrated by 3z^2 versus 2z^2; identify geometrically before normalization. Relative envelopes still use reduced Chow representatives and the integral incidence theorem. Appendix C begins total lambda/exterior-power and K-Euler identities from the same actual K0 relation; these do not replace generation or determine a canonical pathwise surjection."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:11:04.260029+00:00",
          "sheet": 33,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            65,
            66
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "b150a270b8cedecdfc9aa14921f3c55aee87740cc0c5f39ea20064aabd069dc8",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "ae30f25534fe50c599d1b6c1780a55c89d72346c8389e5caef70199eb09a6ac2",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 65–66. Read Proposition C.1's whole pathwise exact-sequence proof: every directed cycle has zero kernel ranks and isomorphism edges, integral source/drain flow decomposes into paths and disposable cycles, and each reversed bundle-surjection path gives a filtered kernel. The divergence bundle is fixed but the surjection and filtration are generally noncanonical. Read Proposition C.2's full DAG path-cone argument, including subtraction at positive-edge sinks, primitive paths with no internal allowed-supply vertices, extremality, unique minimal integral Hilbert basis and semigroup saturation. Cohen–Macaulayness imports Hochster. Read Proposition C.3's integer-decomposition proof for bounded integral incidence-matrix polytopes using the totally unimodular polytope of y in P with x-y in (m-1)P. These are source-proved combinatorial refinements, with no new book admission or independent verifier promotion. Appendix D's functoriality/positivity distinction begins at the page end."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:11:25.482081+00:00",
          "sheet": 34,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            67,
            68
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "4ef06e7fdffcd50bb101acfb126bbc2e75fe991db22db04c98909d21d605aa1b",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "f563e8c2a6b0fc9c64c413b7ffabc00da6072967735f8e4314fa9622de131cd2",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 67–68. Read Proposition D.1's entire class-valued Hankel proof: finite capped A-free tests identify the scalar multiplication-annihilator with the kernel of the A-linear Hankel map, and coefficient maps give canonical injective/surjective moment maps without assuming top-degree equality. Tensor base change has the exact Tor_1(coker H,A') kernel and is an isomorphism for flat A'. No Lefschetz cone is prescribed by these algebraic maps. Example D.2's nonflat P2-to-line restriction has dimensions three versus two and a square-zero z-2h kernel; the free dual-number extension has Hilbert vector (1,3,3,1). Read Proposition D.3's full insertion argument: the correct quotient is by Ann_R(theta), rather than the smaller ideal generated by Ann_A(theta), and it needs no flatness. Active-index shifts remain distinct from fixed insertion. Tensor products of separate moment functionals reconstruct tensor duality quotients, while the coefficient tensor algebra need not be the full diagonal Hodge ring of a product variety."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:12:02.293301+00:00",
          "sheet": 35,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            69,
            70
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "7da9adba02c529a11fe773797e1e5802182fbbca40e0c0c6b768638ecf7a7af0",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "cd42a6a9ae7ef243cf9402cc4804290fe1d6d1a9875449b481c89a922854d366",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 69–70. Read Proposition D.4's full certificate-rank compression: the monic relation factors by xi^(S-s), cancellation occurs in the polynomial ring even with nilpotent coefficient classes, fibre extraction agrees and nonzero boundary descent gives positivity at s0=max(2,d). This compresses certificate algebras, not actual evaluation kernels. Proposition D.5 inserts active relative monomials and gives a weighted base quotient only at coordinatewise maximal nonzero Chern indices. Read Proposition D.6's whole lowering-operator hull proof: stable graded algebras decompose into ambient primitive sl2 strings with definite restricted forms; any same-dimension PD subalgebra containing the interior L inherits HL/HR and is lowering-stable, yielding minimality and independence of the initial interior choice. Example D.7 has source Hilbert vector (1,2,3,3,1), enlarged hull (1,3,4,3,1), dimension twelve inside sixteen and deg a^2bc=2; its finite algebra computation awaits diagnostics. The hull is relative to (R,S), need not be degree-one-generated, and ordinary apolar reconstruction still requires that hypothesis. The projection formula starts at the page end."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:12:23.237529+00:00",
          "sheet": 36,
          "source_id": "Chern_flow_2609.02850v4",
          "physical_pages": [
            71,
