          "source_PDF_SHA256": "104cf0d48495ae1427ec3653ada990cc12738aedb23e27c7ca69f8bd93abecc5",
          "image_SHA256": "aeb1ddec11cf508645ed295890fa8b55214be2545bb586804a918c394904763a",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "280d42e3f50e484d6a655ce896e39167aa0931f7ed9c40200ce025fec23449b2",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read the complete text and individually inspected the matching image for physical pages 71–72. Completed the hull projection: perfect pairings give a graded T-linear idempotent, compatible with nested projections and lowering for interior L, but generally not multiplicative. Read Propositions D.8–D.9 fully. On P2 formal Chern data have the prescribed intrinsic surface Hodge cone exactly for a>=0 and 0<=b<=a^2. The integral (a,b)=(3,1) has a rank-two virtual K0 lift and nonnegative low-degree Schur classes, but a hypothetical generated actual rank-two bundle would give a one-point regular zero and an extension by I_p(3); its explicit two-term resolution gives Ext^1=0, contradicting local freeness. This fixes the original surface, divisor and rank and excludes no scalar realization on another source. Read the AI-use disclosure; it does not supply mathematical proof certification. Read reference entries 1–21, including the exact braid, Lorentzian, historical conjecture and GHMSW sources. Remaining bibliography/dependency pins follow on pages 73–74."
        },
